    "q-76946": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76946",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$67\\text{ mod }6=$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $67$ modulo $6$ is the integer $0\\le r<6$ such that\n\n$$\n67≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $67$ as an integer multiple of $6,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $67≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ because\n\n$$\n67=11\\cdot 6+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $67$ modulo $6$ is $1.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}67 & ≡67-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡67-11\\cdot 6 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡67-66 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡1 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $67$ modulo $6$ is $1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-76946-a",
