    "q-76947": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76947",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$52\\text{ mod }5=$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $52$ modulo $5$ is the integer $0\\le r<5$ such that\n\n$$\n52≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $52$ as an integer multiple of $5,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $52≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ because\n\n$$\n52=10\\cdot 5+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $52$ modulo $5$ is $2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}52 & ≡52-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡52-10\\cdot 5 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡52-50 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡2 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $52$ modulo $5$ is $2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
