    "q-213027": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213027",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$14\\text{ mod }6=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $14$ modulo $6$ is the integer $0\\le r<6$ such that\n\n$$\n14≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $14$ as an integer multiple of $6,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $14≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ because\n\n$$\n14=2\\cdot 6+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $14$ modulo $6$ is $2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & ≡14-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡14-2\\cdot 6 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡14-12 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡2 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $14$ modulo $6$ is $2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
