    "q-213046": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213046",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$27\\text{ mod }4=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $27$ modulo $4$ is the integer $0\\le r<4$ such that\n\n$$\n27≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $27$ as an integer multiple of $4,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $27≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$ because\n\n$$\n27=6\\cdot 4+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $27$ modulo $4$ is $3.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27 & ≡27-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\  & ≡27-6\\cdot 4 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\  & ≡27-24 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\  & ≡3 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $27$ modulo $4$ is $3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
