    "q-76960": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76960",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$-9\\text{ mod }4=$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $-9$ modulo $4$ is the integer $0\\le r<4$ such that\n\n$$\n-9≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-9$ as an integer multiple of $4,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-9≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$ because\n\n$$\n-9=(-3)\\cdot 4+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-9$ modulo $4$ is $3.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9 & ≡-9+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\  & ≡-9+3\\cdot 4 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\  & ≡-9+12 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\  & ≡3 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-9$ modulo $4$ is $3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
