    "q-212004": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212004",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Let $a$ be a positive integer. Construct an expression that gives the last digit of $a.$\n\n$$\na{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let ${d}_{3},$ ${d}_{2},$ and ${d}_{1}$ be the last three digits of the number $a:$ \n\n$$\na=…{d}_{3}{d}_{2}{d}_{1}\n$$\n\nThen, $a$ can be written in expanded form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⋯+100{d}_{3}+10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} \\\\  & =10(⋯+10{d}_{3}+{d}_{2})+{d}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the residue of $a$ modulo $10:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & ≡10(⋯+10{d}_{3}+{d}_{2})+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡0\\cdot (⋯+10{d}_{3}+{d}_{2})+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡0+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${d}_{1}$ is the last digit of $a.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that gives the last digit of $a$ is the following:\n\n$$\na\\,\\text{mod}\\,10\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
